A||||1||loafer87gt||Upgrading computer. Looking for Motherboard suggestions||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||12-07-2001||07:41 PM||||Hey guys, I have to upgrade my rendering machine before the end of the year so I can claim it as a tax write off. I am upgrading from an old T-bird 1.2 /Asus A7v133, and want to make the jump to a DDR MB. Anyone have some suggestions? I did some digging around and found good reviews, as expected, for the Asus and Abit boards, as well as a couple manufacturers I have never heard of before. The one manufacturer that seemed to get very high review and accolades is the SOLTEK SL-75DRV2 board. Anyone on the forum used one of these? I decided to go for an Athlon XP 1700+, as it seems to be the sweet spot pricing wise. I also got a heck of a deal on a ATA 100 Western Digital E-IDE 100 Gig 7200 RPM drive, it should be a lot faster than my ancient 5400 16 gig drive. For graphics I have preordered a FireGL8700 vid card. It is kinda like an ultra version of the Radeon 8500 card, but the drivers are done by the folks at FireGL so they should be rock solid for OpenGL work. Finally, for ram, I ended up going for just 512 megs of Crucial DDR memory. My new 3d program reccommends 2 gig of ram, but with the prices for ram being fairly high at the moment I am going to wait till after christmas and hope that prices drop. Any suggestions or things that you guys would change?||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||12-07-2001||08:47 PM||||Try <A HREF="http://www.tigerdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tigerdirect.com</A>  they seem to have a nice selection of mother boards. Im looking at the SOYO Dragon Plus ATX Socket A with the AMD XP 1800+ chip and 256MB PNY DDR memory, and a GeForce 3 AGP with 64MB of DDR memory. Check them out anyway they have some good deals on stuff. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
